%U A398744 1536,3072,3072,3072,3072,6144,6144,12288,12288,12288,12288,24576,24576,24576
%N A398744 a(n) represents the number of ways to tile a strip of length n with squares (length 1) and dominos (length 2) such that dominos are only placed on prime-numbered cells (0-based indexing).
%F A398744 a(0) = a(1) = 1; a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-2) if n-2 is prime, otherwise a(n) = a(n-1), for n >= 2.
%e A398744 Say you have a strip of length n=4. There is only one possible position for the domino at (n=2), which means there's one tiling with the domino (1 domino 2 squares). You can also tile the strip with only squares (1 tiling). In total, there are two tilings.
